<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Alpha yr shr dips but div raised.</title>
<headline>Alpha yr shr dips but div raised.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - historic cost	 765.7	 vs 773.2</p>
<p>    - current cost	  563.6	 vs 573.1</p>
<p>    Total div (cts)	 280.0	 vs 260.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   169.50	vs 172.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   250.24	vs 323.62</p>
<p>    Tax			 19.31	 vs 90.85</p>
<p>    Borrowing costs	 24.20	 vs 7.87</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,727.59    vs 1,453.93</p>
<p>Full name: Alpha Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the dividend, which has already been proposed, would be declared before the end of April.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share rising to between 793 and 854 cents with consensus pegged at 823.3 cents. They expected a dividend of around 260 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
